{"id":"mahabharata-6-069","work":"mahabharata","part":6,"partName":"भीष्मपर्व","partNameEn":"Bhishma Parva","unit":69,"title":"एकोनसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 69 · Fifth day: Virata and Bhishma","summary":{"en":"Virata and Bhishma exchange arrows, and the heroes praise Arjuna and Krishna for their feats. Bhishma then slaughters the Pandava army with divine weapons until the earth is covered with the fallen.","kn":"ವಿರಾಟ ಮತ್ತು ಭೀಷ್ಮ ಬಾಣ ವಿನಿಮಯ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ; ವೀರರು ಅರ್ಜುನ-ಕೃಷ್ಣರ ಸಾಹಸವನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಬಳಿಕ ಭೀಷ್ಮ ದಿವ್ಯಾಸ್ತ್ರಗಳಿಂದ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಕೊಂದು ಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನು ಶವಗಳಿಂದ ತುಂಬಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"विराट और भीष्म बाणों का आदान-प्रदान करते हैं, और वीर अर्जुन-कृष्ण के पराक्रम की प्रशंसा करते हैं। फिर भीष्म दिव्यास्त्रों से पाण्डव सेना का संहार करते हैं और धरती गिरे हुए योद्धाओं से ढक जाती है।","te":"విరాటుడు, భీష్ముడు బాణాలు మార్చుకుంటారు; వీరులు అర్జున కృష్ణుల పరాక్రమాన్ని ప్రశంసిస్తారు. తరువాత భీష్ముడు దివ్యాస్త్రాలతో పాండవసేనను నరికి భూమిని పడిన వారితో నింపుతాడు.","ta":"விராடனும் பீஷ்மரும் அம்புகள் பரிமாறுகின்றனர்; வீரர்கள் அர்ஜுனன், கண்ணனின் சாதனைகளைப் புகழ்கின்றனர். பின் பீஷ்மர் தெய்வீக அஸ்திரங்களால் பாண்டவப் படையை அழித்து நிலத்தை வீழ்ந்தவர்களால் மூடுகிறார்.","ml":"വിരാടനും ഭീഷ്മരും അമ്പുകൾ കൈമാറുന്നു; അർജുനന്റെയും കൃഷ്ണന്റെയും വീരകൃത്യങ്ങളെ യോദ്ധാക്കൾ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു. പിന്നീട് ഭീഷ്മർ ദിവ്യാസ്ത്രങ്ങൾകൊണ്ട് പാണ്ഡവ സേനയെ കൂട്ടക്കൊല ചെയ്യുന്നു; ഭൂമി വീണവരെക്കൊണ്ട് നിറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 6.69; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Jul 26 2021","sections":[{"title":"भीष्मवधपर्व","titleEn":"Bhishmavadha Parva (The fall of Bhishma)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"विराटोऽथ त्रिभिर्बाणैर्भीष्ममार्छन्महारथम् ।\nविव्याध तुरगांश्चास्य त्रिभिर्बाणैर्महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata struck the great chariot-warrior Bhishma with three arrows, and the great chariot-warrior also pierced his horses with three arrows."}},{"n":2,"text":"तं प्रत्यविध्यद्दशभिर्भीष्मः शांतनवः शरैः ।\nरुक्मपुङ्खैर्महेष्वासः कृतहस्तो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma, Shantanu's son, the great archer, strong and skilled of hand, struck him back with ten gold-feathered arrows."}},{"n":3,"text":"द्रौणिर्गाण्डीवधन्वानं भीमधन्वा महारथः ।\nअविध्यदिषुभिः षड्भिर्दृढहस्तः स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son, the great chariot-warrior with a terrible bow and firm hands, pierced the wielder of Gandiva in the chest with six arrows."}},{"n":4,"text":"कार्मुकं तस्य चिच्छेद फल्गुनः परवीरहा ।\nअविध्यच्च भृशं तीक्ष्णैः पत्रिभिः शत्रुकर्शनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Phalguna, slayer of enemy heroes, cut his bow and, tormenting his foe, struck him hard with sharp, feathered arrows."}},{"n":5,"text":"सोऽन्यत्कार्मुकमादाय वेगवत्क्रोधमूर्छितः ।\nअमृष्यमाणः पार्थेन कार्मुकच्छेदमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up another swift bow, stunned with rage and unable to bear Partha's cutting his bow in the battle,"}},{"n":6,"text":"अविध्यत्फल्गुनं राजन्नवत्या निशितैः शरैः ।\nवासुदेवं च सप्तत्या विव्याध परमेषुभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"he pierced Phalguna with ninety sharp arrows, king, and pierced Vasudeva with seventy supreme arrows."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः क्रोधाभिताम्राक्षः सह कृष्णेन फल्गुनः ।\nदीर्घमुष्णं च निःश्वस्य चिन्तयित्वा मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Phalguna, with Krishna, his eyes coppery with anger, sighing long and hot and thinking again and again,"}},{"n":8,"text":"धनुः प्रपीड्य वामेन करेणामित्रकर्शनः ।\nगाण्डीवधन्वा संक्रुद्धः शितान्संनतपर्वणः ।\nजीवितान्तकरान्घोरान्समादत्त शिलीमुखान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"pressing his bow with his left hand, the tormentor of foes, the enraged wielder of Gandiva, took up sharp, smooth-jointed, terrible arrows that bring an end to life."}},{"n":9,"text":"तैस्तूर्णं समरेऽविध्यद्द्रौणिं बलवतां वरम् ।\nतस्य ते कवचं भित्त्वा पपुः शोणितमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"With these he quickly struck Drona's son, the best of the strong, in the battle; and breaking his armor, they drank his blood in the fight."}},{"n":10,"text":"न विव्यथे च निर्भिन्नो द्रौणिर्गाण्डीवधन्वना ।\nतथैव शरवर्षाणि प्रतिमुञ्चन्नविह्वलः ।\nतस्थौ स समरे राजंस्त्रातुमिच्छन्महाव्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona's son, pierced by the wielder of Gandiva, did not waver; just the same, he loosed showers of arrows, unshaken, and stood in the battle, king, wishing to protect the one of great vows."}},{"n":11,"text":"तस्य तत्सुमहत्कर्म शशंसुः पुरुषर्षभाः ।\nयत्कृष्णाभ्यां समेताभ्यां नापत्रपत संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bulls among men praised that great deed of his, that he felt no shame in the battle against the two Krishnas together."}},{"n":12,"text":"स हि नित्यमनीकेषु युध्यतेऽभयमास्थितः ।\nअस्त्रग्रामं ससंहारं द्रोणात्प्राप्य सुदुर्लभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He always fights in the armies without fear, having obtained from Drona the hard-to-get multitude of weapons with their withdrawal."}},{"n":13,"text":"ममायमाचार्यसुतो द्रोणस्यातिप्रियः सुतः ।\nब्राह्मणश्च विशेषेण माननीयो ममेति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"He is my teacher's son, the dearest son of Drona, and a brahmin, who must especially be honored by me,\" Arjuna thought."}},{"n":14,"text":"समास्थाय मतिं वीरो बीभत्सुः शत्रुतापनः ।\nकृपां चक्रे रथश्रेष्ठो भारद्वाजसुतं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero Bibhatsu, scorcher of foes, best of charioteers, holding to that decision, showed mercy toward Drona's son."}},{"n":15,"text":"द्रौणिं त्यक्त्वा ततो युद्धे कौन्तेयः शत्रुतापनः ।\nयुयुधे तावकान्निघ्नंस्त्वरमाणः पराक्रमी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving Drona's son in the battle, the Kaunteya, scorcher of foes, valiant and swift, fought on, killing your warriors."}},{"n":16,"text":"दुर्योधनस्तु दशभिर्गार्ध्रपत्रैः शिलाशितैः ।\nभीमसेनं महेष्वासं रुक्मपुङ्खैः समर्पयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana pierced the great archer Bhimasena with ten vulture-feathered, stone-whetted, gold-feathered arrows."}},{"n":17,"text":"भीमसेनस्तु संक्रुद्धः परासुकरणं दृढम् ।\nचित्रं कार्मुकमादत्त शरांश्च निशितान्दश ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, enraged, took up a splendid bow, a firm destroyer of life, and ten sharp arrows."}},{"n":18,"text":"आकर्णप्रहितैस्तीक्ष्णैर्वेगितैस्तिग्मतेजनैः ।\nअविध्यत्तूर्णमव्यग्रः कुरुराजं महोरसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"With sharp, swift, keen arrows drawn to the ear, he quickly and calmly struck the king of the Kurus in the broad chest."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्य काञ्चनसूत्रस्तु शरैः परिवृतो मणिः ।\nरराजोरसि वै सूर्यो ग्रहैरिव समावृतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His jewel strung with gold thread, surrounded by arrows, shone on his chest like the sun among planets."}},{"n":20,"text":"पुत्रस्तु तव तेजस्वी भीमसेनेन ताडितः ।\nनामृष्यत यथा नागस्तलशब्दं समीरितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your glorious son, struck by Bhimasena, did not tolerate it, as an elephant cannot bear the sound of a clap."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः शरैर्महाराज रुक्मपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ।\nभीमं विव्याध संक्रुद्धस्त्रासयानो वरूथिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, great king, enraged, he struck Bhima with gold-feathered arrows whetted on stone, terrifying the army."}},{"n":22,"text":"तौ युध्यमानौ समरे भृशमन्योन्यविक्षतौ ।\nपुत्रौ ते देवसंकाशौ व्यरोचेतां महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Fighting in the battle, much wounded by each other, your two mighty sons, like gods, shone."}},{"n":23,"text":"चित्रसेनं नरव्याघ्रं सौभद्रः परवीरहा ।\nअविध्यद्दशभिर्बाणैः पुरुमित्रं च सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Subhadra's son, slayer of enemy heroes, struck Chitrasena, tiger among men, with ten arrows and Purumitra with seven."}},{"n":24,"text":"सत्यव्रतं च सप्तत्या विद्ध्वा शक्रसमो युधि ।\nनृत्यन्निव रणे वीर आर्तिं नः समजीजनत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced Satyavrata with seventy in the battle, the hero like Shakra, seeming to dance in the fight, caused us distress."}},{"n":25,"text":"तं प्रत्यविद्यद्दशभिश्चित्रसेनः शिलीमुखैः ।\nसत्यव्रतश्च नवभिः पुरुमित्रश्च सप्तभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chitrasena struck him back with ten arrows, Satyavrata with nine, and Purumitra with seven."}},{"n":26,"text":"स विद्धो विक्षरन्रक्तं शत्रुसंवारणं महत् ।\nचिच्छेद चित्रसेनस्य चित्रं कार्मुकमार्जुनिः ।\nभित्त्वा चास्य तनुत्राणं शरेणोरस्यताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded, streaming blood, Arjuna's son cut Chitrasena's splendid bow, a great protection against enemies, and, piercing his armor, struck him in the chest with an arrow."}},{"n":27,"text":"ततस्ते तावका वीरा राजपुत्रा महारथाः ।\nसमेत्य युधि संरब्धा विव्यधुर्निशितैः शरैः ।\nतांश्च सर्वाञ्शरैस्तीक्ष्णैर्जघान परमास्त्रवित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your great chariot-warrior heroes, the princes, came together in the battle, enraged, and pierced him with sharp arrows; and he, a master of the highest weapons, struck them all with sharp arrows."}},{"n":28,"text":"तस्य दृष्ट्वा तु तत्कर्म परिवव्रुः सुतास्तव ।\nदहन्तं समरे सैन्यं तव कक्षं यथोल्बणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his deed, your sons surrounded him as he burned your army in the battle, like a fire burning dry grass."}},{"n":29,"text":"अपेतशिशिरे काले समिद्धमिव पावकः ।\nअत्यरोचत सौभद्रस्तव सैन्यानि शातयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the cold season is gone, Subhadra's son shone as he cut down your armies, like a fire well kindled."}},{"n":30,"text":"तत्तस्य चरितं दृष्ट्वा पौत्रस्तव विशां पते ।\nलक्ष्मणोऽभ्यपतत्तूर्णं सात्वतीपुत्रमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his conduct, your grandson Lakshmana, lord of the people, quickly attacked the son of the Satvata woman in the battle."}},{"n":31,"text":"अभिमन्युस्तु संक्रुद्धो लक्ष्मणं शुभलक्षणम् ।\nविव्याध विशिखैः षड्भिः सारथिं च त्रिभिः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Abhimanyu, enraged, struck Lakshmana of fine marks with six arrows and his charioteer with three."}},{"n":32,"text":"तथैव लक्ष्मणो राजन्सौभद्रं निशितैः शरैः ।\nअविध्यत महाराज तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakshmana likewise, king, struck Subhadra's son with sharp arrows, great king, and it was a marvel."}},{"n":33,"text":"तस्याश्वांश्चतुरो हत्वा सारथिं च महाबलः ।\nअभ्यद्रवत सौभद्रो लक्ष्मणं निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed his four horses and charioteer, the mighty Subhadra's son rushed at Lakshmana with sharp arrows."}},{"n":34,"text":"हताश्वे तु रथे तिष्ठँल्लक्ष्मणः परवीरहा ।\nशक्तिं चिक्षेप संक्रुद्धः सौभद्रस्य रथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing on his chariot with its horses slain, Lakshmana, slayer of enemy heroes, enraged, hurled a spear at Subhadra's chariot."}},{"n":35,"text":"तामापतन्तीं सहसा घोररूपां दुरासदाम् ।\nअभिमन्युः शरैस्तीक्ष्णैश्चिच्छेद भुजगोपमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As it came suddenly, terrible and hard to bear, Abhimanyu cut it like a serpent with sharp arrows."}},{"n":36,"text":"ततः स्वरथमारोप्य लक्ष्मणं गौतमस्तदा ।\nअपोवाह रथेनाजौ सर्वसैन्यस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Gautama (Kripa) put Lakshmana on his own chariot and carried him away from the battle in his chariot while all the army watched."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः समाकुले तस्मिन्वर्तमाने महाभये ।\nअभ्यद्रवञ्जिघांसन्तः परस्परवधैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, in that tumultuous great fear, they rushed at one another, wishing to kill and desiring each other's death."}},{"n":38,"text":"तावकाश्च महेष्वासाः पाण्डवाश्च महारथाः ।\nजुह्वन्तः समरे प्राणान्निजघ्नुरितरेतरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Your great archers and the Pandava great chariot-warriors offered up their lives in the battle and struck each other."}},{"n":39,"text":"मुक्तकेशा विकवचा विरथाश्छिन्नकार्मुकाः ।\nबाहुभिः समयुध्यन्त सृञ्जयाः कुरुभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"With loosened hair, without armor, without chariots, their bows cut, the Srinjayas fought the Kurus with their arms."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततो भीष्मो महाबाहुः पाण्डवानां महात्मनाम् ।\nसेनां जघान संक्रुद्धो दिव्यैरस्त्रैर्महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then mighty-armed Bhishma, enraged, struck down the army of the great-souled Pandavas with divine weapons."}},{"n":41,"text":"हतेश्वरैर्गजैस्तत्र नरैरश्वैश्च पातितैः ।\nरथिभिः सादिभिश्चैव समास्तीर्यत मेदिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"The earth was covered with elephants whose masters were killed, with fallen men and horses, and with chariot-warriors and horsemen."}}]}]}